course: dictionary
lesson: 5528
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer wants. «Mum gave me a lecture about my messy room.» The clues are Mum and messy room, so a lecture here is a long, serious talk telling someone off.
explain: At university, a lecture is a talk given to students to teach them about a subject. «The students sat in the lecture hall and took notes.» The clues are students, notes and lecture hall, so this is the teaching meaning.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Mum gave me a long, serious talk about my messy room» still makes sense, so you have chosen the right meaning.
fact: «Lecture» can be a noun (a lecture) or a verb (to lecture).
fact: «Lecture» means a talk given to a group, especially students at a university, to teach them about a subject.
fact: «Lecture» can also mean a long, serious talk telling someone off or telling them how to behave.
fact: A lecture hall or lecture theatre is a room where lectures are given, and the teacher who gives them is a lecturer.
fact: In French, «la lecture» means reading, so it is a false friend: a long talk in French is «une conférence» or «un cours».
exercise: «Mum gave me a lecture about my messy room.» What does lecture mean here? | *A long, serious talk telling someone off | A book to read at bedtime | A talk to students at a university | A game played outside
exercise: «The students sat in the lecture hall and took notes.» What is a lecture in this sentence? | A test at the end of term | A dance for a big crowd | *A talk given to students to teach them about a subject | A kind of reading book
exercise: «The professor will lecture on history tomorrow.» What does lecture mean in this sentence? | To shout angrily at someone | To read a book aloud | *To give a talk to students on a subject | To clean a room
test: «Dad gave a long lecture about being late.» What does lecture mean here? | *A long, serious talk telling someone off | A short song | A school trip | A kind of cake
test: What does lecture mean in «The lecture hall was full of students with notebooks»? | A loud noise from the street | A dance | A shop that sells notebooks | *A talk for students at a university
exam: Jayden says «lecture» always means a boring talk. Is he right? | Yes, it always means a boring talk | *No, it has more than one meaning, such as a talk for students or a serious telling-off | Yes, and it always means reading in French | No, it only ever means a song
